From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROCK 5B debug kernel <debug-kernel@localhost>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: add persistent ramoops to ROCK 5B

The previous userspace overlay placed ramoops near the top of DRAM.  The
RK3588 boot chain does not preserve that range across reset, so every boot
reported bad ECC headers and pstore was always empty.

Use the low persistent range selected by Rockchip's RK3588 BSP, below the
Linux RAM start at 0x200000.  The BSP dedicates 0x110000-0x1f0000 to ramoops,
uses 0x110000-0x118000 for firmware boot logs, and starts a separate minidump
reservation at 0x1f0000.  Give upstream ramoops 0x118000-0x1e8000, avoiding
both vendor-only areas and leaving the last 32 KiB unassigned.

The selected 832 KiB holds one 256 KiB panic/oops record, a 512 KiB console
record, and a 64 KiB pmsg record.  Keep ECC enabled so genuine corruption is
reported.

Signed-off-by: ROCK 5B debug kernel <debug-kernel@localhost>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts
index da13dafcbc82..9306473bd7bd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts
@@ -7,6 +7,23 @@
 / {
 	model = "Radxa ROCK 5B";
 	compatible = "radxa,rock-5b", "rockchip,rk3588";
+
+	reserved-memory {
+		/*
+		 * The BSP's boot log ends at 0x118000 and its minidump starts
+		 * at 0x1f0000. Linux RAM starts at 0x200000.
+		 */
+		ramoops: ramoops@118000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0x00118000 0x0 0x000d0000>;
+			no-map;
+			record-size = <0x00040000>;
+			console-size = <0x00080000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x00010000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+		};
+	};
+
 };
 
 &sdio {
